/**
@page api_pfqn Product-Form Queueing Networks
@brief MVA, convolution, and normalizing constant methods

The pfqn module contains algorithms for product-form queueing networks, including
Mean Value Analysis (MVA), convolution, and normalizing constant methods.

@subsection product-form_queueing_networks_matlab_src_api_pfqn__list Function List

- @ref pfqn_aql "pfqn_aql" - Approximate Queue Length (AQL) algorithm for product-form networks.
- @ref pfqn_bsfcfs "pfqn_bsfcfs" - Bard-Schweitzer approximate MVA for FCFS scheduling with weighted priorities.
- @ref pfqn_bs "pfqn_bs" - Bard-Schweitzer Approximate Mean Value Analysis (MVA).
- @ref pfqn_ca "pfqn_ca" - Convolution Algorithm for exact normalizing constant computation.
- @ref pfqn_cdfun "pfqn_cdfun" - AMVA-QD class-dependence function for queue-dependent scaling.
- @ref pfqn_comom "pfqn_comom" - CoMoM algorithm for computing the normalizing constant.
- @ref pfqn_comomrm_ld "pfqn_comomrm_ld" - CoMoM for repairman model with load-dependent service rates.
- @ref pfqn_comomrm "pfqn_comomrm" - CoMoM (Convolution Method of Moments) for finite repairman model.
- @ref pfqn_comomrm_ms "pfqn_comomrm_ms" - CoMoM for multiserver repairman model.
- @ref pfqn_comomrm_orig "pfqn_comomrm_orig" - Original CoMoM implementation for finite repairman model.
- @ref pfqn_conwayms "pfqn_conwayms" - Multiserver Linearizer approximation (Conway 1989).
- @ref pfqn_cub "pfqn_cub" - Cubature method for normalizing constant using Grundmann-Moeller rules.
- @ref pfqn_egflinearizer "pfqn_egflinearizer" - Extended generalized fixed-point Linearizer approximation.
- @ref pfqn_fnc "pfqn_fnc" - Generate load-dependent rates for functional server model f(n)=n+c.
- @ref pfqn_gflinearizer "pfqn_gflinearizer" - Generalized fixed-point Linearizer with uniform scaling exponent.
- @ref pfqn_gld "pfqn_gld" - Exact normalizing constant for load-dependent queueing networks.
- @ref pfqn_gldsingle "pfqn_gldsingle" - Exact normalizing constant for single-class load-dependent models.
- @ref pfqn_grnmol "pfqn_grnmol" - Normalizing constant using Grundmann-Moeller quadrature.
- @ref pfqn_joint "pfqn_joint" - Compute joint queue-length probability distribution.
- @ref pfqn_kt "pfqn_kt" - Knessl-Tier asymptotic expansion for normalizing constant.
- @ref pfqn_lap "pfqn_lap" - Laplace approximation for normalizing constant.
- @ref pfqn_lcfsqn_ca "pfqn_lcfsqn_ca" - Convolution algorithm for 2-station LCFS queueing networks
- @ref pfqn_lcfsqn_mva "pfqn_lcfsqn_mva" - Exact MVA for 2-station LCFS queueing networks.
- @ref pfqn_le "pfqn_le" - Logistic expansion (LE) asymptotic approximation for normalizing constant.
- @ref pfqn_linearizer "pfqn_linearizer" - Linearizer approximation for single-server stations.
- @ref pfqn_linearizerms "pfqn_linearizerms" - Multiserver Linearizer (Krzesinski/Conway/De Souza-Muntz).
- @ref pfqn_linearizermx "pfqn_linearizermx" - Linearizer for mixed open/closed queueing networks.
- @ref pfqn_lldfun "pfqn_lldfun" - AMVA-QD load and queue-dependent scaling function.
- @ref pfqn_ls "pfqn_ls" - Logistic sampling approximation for normalizing constant.
- @ref pfqn_mci "pfqn_mci" - Monte Carlo Integration (MCI) for normalizing constant.
- @ref pfqn_mmint2_gausslaguerre "pfqn_mmint2_gausslaguerre" - McKenna-Mitra integral with Gauss-Laguerre quadrature.
- @ref pfqn_mmint2_gausslegendre "pfqn_mmint2_gausslegendre" - McKenna-Mitra integral with Gauss-Legendre quadrature.
- @ref pfqn_mmint2 "pfqn_mmint2" - McKenna-Mitra integral form for repairman models using MATLAB integral.
- @ref pfqn_mmsample2 "pfqn_mmsample2" - Monte Carlo sampling for repairman models using McKenna-Mitra form.
- @ref pfqn_mu_ms "pfqn_mu_ms" - Compute load-dependent rates for m identical c-server FCFS stations.
- @ref pfqn_mushift "pfqn_mushift" - Shift load-dependent service rate vector by removing first element.
- @ref pfqn_mvald "pfqn_mvald" - Exact MVA for load-dependent closed queueing networks.
- @ref pfqn_mvaldms "pfqn_mvaldms" - Load-dependent MVA for multiserver mixed networks (wrapper for pfqn_mvaldmx).
- @ref pfqn_mvaldmx_ec "pfqn_mvaldmx_ec" - Compute effective capacity terms for MVALDMX solver.
- @ref pfqn_mvaldmx "pfqn_mvaldmx" - Load-dependent MVA for mixed open/closed networks with limited load dependence.
- @ref pfqn_mva "pfqn_mva" - Exact Mean Value Analysis (MVA) for product-form queueing networks.
- @ref pfqn_mvams "pfqn_mvams" - General-purpose MVA for mixed networks with multiserver nodes.
- @ref pfqn_mvamx "pfqn_mvamx" - Exact MVA for mixed open/closed single-server networks.
- @ref pfqn_lcfsqn_nc "pfqn_lcfsqn_nc" - Normalizing constant for LCFS queueing networks
- @ref pfqn_ncld "pfqn_ncld" - Normalizing constant for load-dependent closed networks.
- @ref pfqn_nc "pfqn_nc" - Computes the normalizing constant of a product-form queueing network.
- @ref pfqn_nc_sanitize "pfqn_nc_sanitize" - Sanitize and preprocess network parameters for NC solvers.
- @ref pfqn_nrl "pfqn_nrl" - Normalizing constant via Normal Radius-Logistic (NRL) approximation.
- @ref pfqn_nrp "pfqn_nrp" - Normalizing constant via Normal Radius-Probit (NRP) approximation.
- @ref pfqn_panacea "pfqn_panacea" - PANACEA (PAth-based Normal Approximation for Closed networks Estimation Algorithm).
- @ref pfqn_procomom2 "pfqn_procomom2" - Product-form CoMoM for 2-station repairman model (queue + delay).
- @ref pfqn_propfair "pfqn_propfair" - Proportionally fair allocation approximation (Walton 2009).
- @ref pfqn_qd "pfqn_qd" - Queue-Dependent (QD) approximate MVA solver.
- @ref pfqn_qzgblow "pfqn_qzgblow" - Lower asymptotic bound on queue length (Zahorjan-Gittelsohn-Bryant).
- @ref pfqn_qzgbup "pfqn_qzgbup" - Upper asymptotic bound on queue length (Zahorjan-Gittelsohn-Bryant).
- @ref pfqn_rd "pfqn_rd" - Reduced Decomposition (RD) method for load-dependent networks.
- @ref pfqn_recal "pfqn_recal" - RECAL (REcursive CALculation) method for normalizing constant.
- @ref pfqn_schmidt "pfqn_schmidt" - Schmidt's exact MVA for networks with general scheduling disciplines.
- @ref pfqn_sqni "pfqn_sqni" - Single Queue Network Iteration (SQNI) approximate solver.
- @ref pfqn_stdf_heur "pfqn_stdf_heur" - Heuristic sojourn time distribution for multiserver FCFS nodes (McKenna 1987 variant).
- @ref pfqn_stdf "pfqn_stdf" - Sojourn time distribution for multiserver FCFS nodes (McKenna 1987).
- @ref pfqn_xzabalow "pfqn_xzabalow" - Lower asymptotic bound on throughput (Zahorjan-Balanced).
- @ref pfqn_xzabaup "pfqn_xzabaup" - Upper asymptotic bound on throughput (Zahorjan-Balanced).
- @ref pfqn_xzgsblow "pfqn_xzgsblow" - Lower asymptotic bound on throughput (Zahorjan-Gittelsohn-Schweitzer-Bryant).
- @ref pfqn_xzgsbup "pfqn_xzgsbup" - Upper asymptotic bound on throughput (Zahorjan-Gittelsohn-Schweitzer-Bryant).

@anchor pfqn_aql
### pfqn_aql
  <b>Description:</b> Approximate Queue Length (AQL) algorithm for product-form networks.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [XN, QN, UN, RN, numIters, AN] = pfqn_aql(L, N, Z, TOL, MAXITER, QN0)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>TOL</td><td>Tolerance for convergence.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>MAXITER</td><td>Maximum number of iterations.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN0</td><td>Initial guess for queue lengths.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>XN</td><td>System throughput.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN</td><td>Mean queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>UN</td><td>Utilization.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>RN</td><td>Residence times.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>numIters</td><td>Number of iterations.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>AN</td><td>Average arrival rate at nodes.</td></tr>
  </table>

@anchor pfqn_bsfcfs
### pfqn_bsfcfs
  <b>Description:</b> Bard-Schweitzer approximate MVA for FCFS scheduling with weighted priorities.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [XN, QN, UN, RN, it] = pfqn_bsfcfs(L, N, Z, tol, maxiter, QN, weight)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector (default: zeros).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>tol</td><td>Convergence tolerance (default: 1e-6).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>maxiter</td><td>Maximum number of iterations (default: 1000).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN</td><td>Initial queue length matrix (default: uniform distribution).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>weight</td><td>Weight matrix for relative priorities (default: ones).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>XN</td><td>System throughput.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN</td><td>Mean queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>UN</td><td>Utilization.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>RN</td><td>Residence times.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>it</td><td>Number of iterations performed.</td></tr>
  </table>

@anchor pfqn_bs
### pfqn_bs
  <b>Description:</b> Bard-Schweitzer Approximate Mean Value Analysis (MVA).

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [XN, QN, UN, RN, it] = pfqn_bs(L, N, Z, tol, maxiter, QN0, type)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>tol</td><td>Tolerance for convergence.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>maxiter</td><td>Maximum number of iterations.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN0</td><td>Initial guess for queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>type</td><td>Scheduling strategy type (default: PS).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>XN</td><td>System throughput.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN</td><td>Mean queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>UN</td><td>Utilization.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>RN</td><td>Residence times.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>it</td><td>Number of iterations performed.</td></tr>
  </table>

@anchor pfqn_ca
### pfqn_ca
  <b>Description:</b> Convolution Algorithm for exact normalizing constant computation.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
