@anchor pfqn_mva
### pfqn_mva
  <b>Description:</b> Exact Mean Value Analysis (MVA) for product-form queueing networks.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [XN, QN, UN, CN, lGN] = pfqn_mva(L, N, Z, mi)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix (M x R).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector (1 x R).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector (1 x R).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>mi</td><td>(Optional) Server multiplicity vector (1 x M). Default: single servers.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>XN</td><td>System throughput (1 x R).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN</td><td>Mean queue length (M x R).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>UN</td><td>Utilization (M x R).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>CN</td><td>Residence time (M x R).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>lGN</td><td>Logarithm of the normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  </table>

@anchor pfqn_mvams
### pfqn_mvams
  <b>Description:</b> General-purpose MVA for mixed networks with multiserver nodes.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [XN, QN, UN, CN, lG] = pfqn_mvams(lambda, L, N, Z, mi, S)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lambda</td><td>Arrival rate vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>mi</td><td>Queue replication factors (default: ones).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>S</td><td>Number of servers per station (default: ones).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>XN</td><td>System throughput.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN</td><td>Mean queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>UN</td><td>Utilization.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>CN</td><td>Cycle times.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>lG</td><td>Logarithm of normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  </table>

@anchor pfqn_mvamx
### pfqn_mvamx
  <b>Description:</b> Exact MVA for mixed open/closed single-server networks.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [XN, QN, UN, CN, lGN] = pfqn_mvamx(lambda, D, N, Z, mi)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lambda</td><td>Arrival rate vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>D</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>mi</td><td>Queue replication factors (default: ones).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>XN</td><td>System throughput.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QN</td><td>Mean queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>UN</td><td>Utilization.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>CN</td><td>Cycle times.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>lGN</td><td>Logarithm of normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  </table>

@anchor pfqn_lcfsqn_nc
### pfqn_lcfsqn_nc
  <b>Description:</b> Normalizing constant for LCFS queueing networks

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [G, Ax] = pfqn_lcfsqn_nc(alpha, beta, N)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>alpha</td><td>Service rates at LCFS station (1xR vector).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>beta</td><td>Service rates at LCFS-PR station (1xR vector).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector (default: ones(1,R)).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>G</td><td>Normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Ax</td><td>Cell array of A matrices for each state.</td></tr>
  </table>

@anchor pfqn_ncld
### pfqn_ncld
  <b>Description:</b> Normalizing constant for load-dependent closed networks.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [lG, G, method] = pfqn_ncld(L, N, Z, mu, varargin)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>mu</td><td>Load-dependent rate matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>options</td><td>Optional solver parameters.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lG</td><td>Logarithm of normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>G</td><td>Normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>method</td><td>Method used for computation.</td></tr>
  </table>

@anchor pfqn_nc
### pfqn_nc
  <b>Description:</b> Computes the normalizing constant of a product-form queueing network.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [lG, X, Q, method] = pfqn_nc(lambda, L, N, Z, varargin)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lambda</td><td>Arrival rates for open classes.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>options</td><td>Optional arguments for solver options (NC.defaultOptions).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lG</td><td>Logarithm of the normalizing constant.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>X</td><td>System throughputs.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Q</td><td>Mean queue lengths.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>method</td><td>The specific method used for computation (e.g., 'exact', 'ca', 'recal').</td></tr>
  </table>

@anchor pfqn_nc_sanitize
### pfqn_nc_sanitize
  <b>Description:</b> Sanitize and preprocess network parameters for NC solvers.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [lambda, L, N, Z, lGremaind] = pfqn_nc_sanitize(lambda, L, N, Z, atol)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lambda</td><td>Arrival rate vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Service demand matrix.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Population vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Think time vector.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>atol</td><td>Absolute tolerance.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lambda</td><td>Sanitized arrival rates.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>L</td><td>Sanitized service demands (rescaled).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>N</td><td>Sanitized populations.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Z</td><td>Sanitized think times (rescaled).</td></tr>
  <tr><td>lGremaind</td><td>Log normalization factor from removed classes.</td></tr>
  </table>

@anchor pfqn_nrl
### pfqn_nrl
  <b>Description:</b> Normalizing constant via Normal Radius-Logistic (NRL) approximation.

